  "id": "cypriot_violi_laouto",
  "name": "Violi kai laouto (Cypriot fiddle-and-lute dance music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Village music of Greek-speaking Cyprus played by a duo of violin (violi) and laouto lute for weddings, feasts and saints'-day fairs (panigyria). Its repertoire joins the island's dances, among them the syrtos, the kartsilamades couple dances and the tatsia, with the fones, regional melody-types to which singers set traditional or improvised couplets in the fifteen-syllable line. Older ensembles also used the pithkiavli shepherd's flute and the tamboutsia frame drum, and the Cyprus Broadcasting Corporation recorded the repertoire from the mid-twentieth century.",
  "recipe": "classic modern violi kai laouto, wedding, European branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. fiddle, island rhythmic laouto. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
